<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>🌧️ LIVE PRECIPITATION</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/precipitation_na/legend.png" width="600" alt="legend"><br>Precipitation intensity (NEXRAD N0Q base reflectivity, dBZ, OBSERVED radar echo): <b>LOWEST 5 Very Light</b> cyan/blue (drizzle, mist) &rarr; <b>Light</b> greens (~20-30: light rain/snow) &rarr; <b>Moderate</b> dark green (~30-40: steady rain/snow) &rarr; <b>Heavy</b> yellow/orange (~40-50: heavy rain) &rarr; <b>Severe</b> red (~50-60: severe storms, hail possible) &rarr; <b>Intense</b> magenta/purple (~60-70: violent storms, large hail) &rarr; <b>HIGHEST+ 70+ Extreme</b> white (destructive hail, debris). Same dBZ always shows the same color in every season — rain, snow, lake-effect snow, thunderstorms. No echo (no precipitation) stays see-through so the map underneath shows. Measurement types differ by source: IEM N0Q and OPERA are MEASURED reflectivity (dBZ); ECCC rain colors are ESTIMATED dBZ equivalents converted from rain rates via Z=300R^1.4 (ECCC publishes mm/h, not dBZ — high-rate classes saturate near ~57 dBZ, so ECCC never paints the white extreme row); ECCC snow blues are severity-rank matched, not dBZ; pale/muted colors are GFS MODEL estimates (6-h mean rates), never radar. ECCC snow echoes render blue ONLY where SfcPrecipType classifies snow (mixed/freezing rain render on the dBZ key at matched severity). Muted colors = GFS model estimates (same order, not radar).</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: Iowa Environmental Mesonet CONUS NEXRAD N0Q base reflectivity (NOAA WSR-88D) inside its domain + ECCC North American Radar Composite 1km rain (RADAR_1KM_RRAI, mm/h) / snow (RADAR_1KM_RSNO, cm/h) / precipitation type (Radar_1km_SfcPrecipType) outside it + EUMETNET OPERA EU DBZH composite (CC BY 4.0) in remaining radar gaps + NOAA GFS translucent model estimates (public domain) in verified radar gaps only).</p><p>Turn on/off independently of all other layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <NetworkLink>
      <name>🌧️ LIVE PRECIPITATION — auto-refresh</name>
      <Link>
        <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/live/North_America_Live_Precipitation.kml</href>
        <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
        <refreshInterval>300</refreshInterval>
      </Link>
    </NetworkLink>
  </Document>
</kml>
